WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.690
So there's a guy who called into C-SPAN after
the first deranged and depraved evening of

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.510
the Republican National Convention.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:12.570
And the guy called in and said said he's a
lifelong Democrat, but the first night of

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:18.230
the Republican convention has convinced him
to switch his vote and vote for Donald Trump.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.810
Now, I'm going to play the call for you in
a moment, but what I want to raise ahead of

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:26.390
time is in reaction to what I'm about to play
for you.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.630
There's a lot of people who are debating,
is the guy for real or is he a troll?

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.610
Is this for real or is the guy faking?

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:37.200
And he's really a Trump guy who just called
C-SPAN and said that he's a lifelong Democrat.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.320
I have some thoughts about that.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.970
But I'm actually going to make the case that
it doesn't matter.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.970
And I'll explain why.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.640
But first, let's take a look at the video.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.640
Rick in Lorain, Ohio, Democrat.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.410
Hi, Rick.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.890
Tonight, I'm a lifelong Democrat.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.040
I'm from Ohio, which is a Democrat city in
Ohio.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:03.080
And I just want to say, after watching the
convention tonight on TV on C-SPAN here, I

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.830
am definitely changing my vote to Republican.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.930
And I'll tell you what, they just put the
Democratic Party as the Republican Party to

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:12.930
shame.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.300
I'm going to follow the Republican Party now.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.400
But why what what what was it that convinced
you about tonight?

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:24.250
It was the heartfelt way they came across
to the American people.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:29.190
And I was really touched by the number of
times I use the word God.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.670
They put God into everything.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:36.140
And the people on the Democratic side or near
convention act like they were pushing God

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.500
right out of it.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.750
And that's had a lot to do with change in
my mind now.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.690
Rick, did you say you were a union member?

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.690
No, sir.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.110
I'm from Lorain, Ohio.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.490
And we are a Democrat town here and have been
for 50 years.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.490
That's it.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.780
Thank you so much.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:59.260
So in terms of whether this is for real or
where this is, whether this is really a Trump

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:06.830
guy who is lying, that he's a lifelong Democrat,
the guy said that he's calling from a Democrat

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:09.020
city in Ohio.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:15.060
I've never met a lifelong Democrat who calls
cities Democrat cities.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.459
That's how the Wright talks.

00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:21.790
That's literally a term out of Trump's playbook
from the last two or three years.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:27.400
So I think that there's certainly reason to
doubt whether this guy is sincerely a lifelong

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:33.410
Democrat who was convinced to switch and vote
for Trump from night one of the DNC, from

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.230
the RNC, rather.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.430
But it doesn't matter.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.430
Okay.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.670
This is sort of like looking at retail versus
wholesale.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:46.310
The question isn't whether this one guy was
really convinced to vote for Trump because

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.249
of the RNC.

00:02:48.249 --> 00:02:54.380
Someone in a country of 331 million people
with 120 to 135 million expected to vote,

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.260
someone I'm sure is going to be convinced
to vote.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:02.920
Trump, who was previously thinking they were
going to go vote Biden by the RNC.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.659
The point is the big picture first, it's the
big picture of conventions.

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:11.269
If history is an indicator, conventions don't
really do much for either candidate.

00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:16.139
Typically, what you see is one candidate has
a convention and they get a little bump and

00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:20.049
then the other candidate has a convention
and they get a little bump and then it fades.

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:21.879
And by October, nobody remembers it.

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:23.750
And we've moved on to other things.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:28.989
The right has tried to make the case that
there is a massive movement of Democrats abandoning

00:03:28.989 --> 00:03:32.870
the Democratic Party and jumping ship to vote
for Donald Trump.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.689
It's not backed up by the data that we have.

00:03:34.689 --> 00:03:39.379
There is no doubt that there are disaffected
Democrats who don't like the fact that Joe

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:40.629
Biden is a candidate.

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:41.849
Some of them are going to stay home.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:43.819
Some of them are going to vote for Donald
Trump.

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:48.420
Likewise, there are people who voted Trump
in 2016 who are going to vote for Biden.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:54.040
There is no evidence right now that there
are large numbers of Democrats defecting to

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.879
the Republican Party or planning to vote for
Donald Trump.

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:03.659
The one caller is not really newsworthy, but
there is the more interesting.

00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:08.280
Deeper question about the bigger picture here,
which is, are people switching parties?

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.769
What we know is that most 2016 Trump voters
are going to vote for Trump again.

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:18.010
What we know is that most 2016 Hillary voters
are going to vote for Biden.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.680
What we know is that independents are leaning
towards Joe Biden.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:27.310
And ultimately, this is going to come down
to who votes in which states and how much

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.930
of the vote can Donald Trump suppress.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:36.349
So maybe it's true that this particular guy
was a lifelong Democrat and he was convinced

00:04:36.349 --> 00:04:40.780
after a life of voting for Democrats to vote
for Donald Trump because of Kimberly Guilfoyle

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:45.849
screaming on Monday night at the Republican
National Convention, or as he says, because

00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:49.110
the Republican convention kept mentioning
God.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.449
The truth, of course, is that in reality,
Joe Biden is more religious than Donald Trump.

00:04:53.449 --> 00:04:55.639
It's not something I care about.

00:04:55.639 --> 00:05:00.870
But for people who want a religious candidate,
there's no question that Donald Trump's religiosity

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:05.569
is completely fabricated and fake as something
to appeal to evangelical voters.

00:05:05.569 --> 00:05:10.699
With Trump as a politician, whereas Joe Biden
actually seems to be a moderate, moderately

00:05:10.699 --> 00:05:12.979
devout Catholic, I don't care about that.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.400
But if you're looking for the religious candidate,
it's not Donald Trump.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.129
It's Joe Biden up.

00:05:17.129 --> 00:05:20.470
But sure, the caller might be making it up
as well.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:24.960
It doesn't matter if we all go out and vote,
period.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.490
And that is ultimately going to be the ones
has it.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.690
It's not.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.159
Did this guy switch in Ohio, by the way?

00:05:32.159 --> 00:05:33.159
Ohio.

00:05:33.159 --> 00:05:37.400
Not looking as good for Joe Biden as it did
before, or I guess better said, looking better

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.280
for Donald Trump recently than it did before.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.370
What matters is if we all go out and vote
and the large numbers and so I wouldn't be

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:49.020
lulled into a false debate about whether it's
possible that the RNC really shifted a Democrat

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.020
into voting for Trump.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:55.860
I'm sure some Democrats did get convinced
to vote Trump from the RNC and some Republicans

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.569
were convinced to vote for Joe Biden from
the DNC.

00:05:58.569 --> 00:06:00.680
We're a country of 300 and 31 million.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.629
The big picture is what matters.

00:06:02.629 --> 00:06:06.539
Let's not lose sight of that in the big picture
is Trump's going to try to win by suppressing

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:07.879
the vote.

00:06:07.879 --> 00:06:10.189
Trump's going to try to win by rigging the
election.

00:06:10.189 --> 00:06:11.570
That's the big picture.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:33.250
Not whether this

00:06:33.250 --> 00:07:05.180
guy

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:20.710
is

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:36.149
a troll.

